# --- Python ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# --- Build outputs ---
# Keep ALL build output out of the repo, including the installer. Committing a
# 70 MB binary on every build grew .git to 2.75 GB (each build stored a fresh
# blob that binaries cannot delta). The installer is a RELEASE artefact: build
# it with build.bat and attach it to a tagged GitHub Release instead. The file
# still appears on disk in dist\ after every build - it is simply not tracked.
/dist/
/build/
/specfiles/
*.spec

# --- Downloaded prerequisites ---
# vc_redist.x64.exe (~24 MB) is committed so offline builds/releases need no
# re-download; build.bat only re-downloads it when the file is missing.
# (deliberately NOT ignored)

# --- Runtime artifacts: raw captures & logs, generated while connected ---
*.log
*.csv
# ...but keep the bundled replay fixture:
!sample.log

# --- Internal handoff notes (kept local, not published) ---
/internal/
/AGENTS.md

# --- Generated at build time by make_release_notes.py from CHANGELOG.md;
# shipped inside the installer for the once-per-update popup ---
/releasenotes.py

# --- OS / editor cruft ---

Thumbs.db
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
